{"id": "EUVD-2026-93350", "enisaUuid": "25a36082-311e-38bf-9080-5c1e28afb7f9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/rxe: Fix integer overflow in mr_check_range() leading to OOB access\n\nmr_check_range() validates that [iova, iova+length) falls within the\nregistered MR range using wraparound-prone arithmetic:\n\n    if (iova < mr->ibmr.iova ||\n        iova + length > mr->ibmr.iova + mr->ibmr.length)\n\nA remote peer can craft an RDMA-Write/Read RETH so that iova + length\nwraps to 0 (e.g. iova=0xfffffffffffffff8, length=8), bypassing the\ncheck. rxe_mr_iova_to_index() then computes a huge index (int idx, only\nguarded by WARN_ON) and rxe_mr_copy_xarray() dereferences\nmr->page_info[huge], causing an out-of-bounds read/write and a kernel\noops that is triggerable by an unauthenticated remote peer.\n\nRewrite the check in overflow-safe form; the first two clauses guarantee\nthat the subsequent subtractions do not underflow:\n\n    if (iova < mr->ibmr.iova ||\n        length > mr->ibmr.length ||\n        iova - mr->ibmr.iova > mr->ibmr.length - length)\n\nWith the fix, mr_check_range() returns -EINVAL for the crafted iova and\nthe responder reports REMOTE_ACCESS_ERROR instead of triggering the OOB.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:18:17", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b7d2118660545a00b21e83010ded1a231c6fb8c5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5d9426a74fc8cb8f375fcdc19b465a030f9b8cab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f3b705144e3a3c14184fec6e354680081fe91ec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3431f525718f6b07da308cda6d44f8cb548bbd37", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d10e2a08799e858d3e71ea4169bcd018f216d444"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98365", "GHSA-3p8h-wx5x-6qq3"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.38, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1a5ee0f5-1723-340d-95bd-c1356c18a616", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8700e3e7c4857d28ebaa824509934556da0b3e76 <d10e2a08799e858d3e71ea4169bcd018f216d444"}, {"id": "4aa53db5-667a-3d12-900b-bbeb5ed3d370", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4e96b71e-2a78-35ab-9e87-34437e1eee25", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5797ffb9-1e94-3413-af5e-6f3636862db0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "5c334496-facf-39ee-a3ae-8e7d70f425c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8700e3e7c4857d28ebaa824509934556da0b3e76 <3431f525718f6b07da308cda6d44f8cb548bbd37"}, {"id": "60a8a25a-0516-32a6-9c12-a6fdccf61320", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.8"}, {"id": "66548133-7fb0-3a72-b509-b96022c1e9aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "893423b9-915f-3e09-947d-6a27da6ec18c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "a3eb0a82-77ad-3afd-9480-3882fcb10497", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "a4d35d6c-0a18-305a-8c38-e607372ad3c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8700e3e7c4857d28ebaa824509934556da0b3e76 <2f3b705144e3a3c14184fec6e354680081fe91ec"}, {"id": "c6422e88-ea78-35a1-a4bf-40db675ddba1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8700e3e7c4857d28ebaa824509934556da0b3e76 <b7d2118660545a00b21e83010ded1a231c6fb8c5"}, {"id": "f8b980b3-b7b8-396b-ba3a-ea508921530f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8700e3e7c4857d28ebaa824509934556da0b3e76 <5d9426a74fc8cb8f375fcdc19b465a